{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1770","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1770","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1770\",\"parent_revision\":\"5b46d0c528372f8bf20a7ad8e2773a0e4312b3de0193e013b86cdc8fb9dab582\",\"root_revision\":\"5b46d0c528372f8bf20a7ad8e2773a0e4312b3de0193e013b86cdc8fb9dab582\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P0\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-02\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n# Make SAM plans granular \u2014 incremental task append instead of monolithic create\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM: `_sam_plan_create` at `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` lines 271-296 parses a single `tasks_yaml` string and calls `backend.create_plan(slug, goal, tasks=task_defs, context, issue)` atomically.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:271-296\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-12\\n  - Content: |\\n      def _sam_plan_create(config: CreatePlanConfig, plan_dir: str) -> dict:\\n          \\\"\\\"\\\"Create a new plan from YAML task definitions. ...\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n          yaml_parser: Any = YAML()\\n          parsed: dict[str, Any] = yaml_parser.load(config.tasks_yaml)\\n          if not isinstance(parsed, dict) or \\\"tasks\\\" not in parsed:\\n              raise ValueError(\\\"tasks_yaml must be a YAML string with a top-level 'tasks' key\\\")\\n          task_defs = cast(\\\"list[TaskDefinition]\\\", parsed[\\\"tasks\\\"])\\n          backend = _get_backend(plan_dir)\\n          plan_data = backend.create_plan(\\n              slug=config.slug, goal=config.goal, tasks=task_defs, context=config.context, issue=config.issue\\n          )\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `_sam_plan_update` at lines 363-377 calls `backend.update_plan_fields(plan, context, set_fields)` and never touches tasks.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - So