DERIVABLE count: 11 (10 original + 1 new \u2014 condition 20)\\nMISSING count: 0\\nINFORMATIONAL count: 2 (condition 19 documented coverage gap, condition 21 redundancy note)\\n\\n**Verdict: APPROVED** \u2014 All original MISSING conditions remain resolved. New conditions discovered during implementation are either RESOLVED, DOCUMENTED, or TRACEABLE to specific commits. No new MISSING conditions.\\n\\n**Changes from 2026-04-12 snapshot**:\\n- Conditions 1-4 upgraded from AVAILABLE to CONFIRMED via implementation evidence\\n- Conditions 5-13 resolved via specific commits (cited)\\n- Conditions 14-15 documented as implemented (were user-resolved)\\n- Conditions 16-17 resolved via red phase + green phase\\n- New conditions 18-22 added covering implementation-time discoveries\\n- Verdict stays APPROVED; ready for Wave 5 T12 verification + T13 close-out + Wave 6 T14 + /dh:complete-implementation\\n\\n**Outstanding work before item can transition to DONE**:\\n- Wave 5 T12: verify drafting guards in `_sam_plan_status` and `_sam_plan_ready`; add if absent\\n- Wave 5 T13: close as redundant with T2+T3+T6, OR verify `_sam_plan_create` server-side injection isn't needed\\n- Wave 6 T14: remove 22 xfail markers + fix the broken mock on `test_sam_append_task_routes_through_backend_append_task`\\n- /dh:complete-implementation: run quality gates + forensic review + final verification against the 19 ACs\\n- Merge PR #1773 once all checks go green\\n- Follow-up backlog items #1774 and #1775 remain open for separate grooming\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py::TaskBackend` - Protocol must gain a new `append_task` method; every concrete backend must implement it or the Protocol is violated | Risk: HIGH | Why: Protocol addition propagates to all three backends; GitHub backend is partially implemented and any gap silently breaks the feature for that provider\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py::PlanActionConfig` - Discriminated union must include a new `AppendTaskConfig` variant (or equivalent) and add it to `PlanActionConfig`; `CreatePlanConfig` description field `tasks_yaml` may need updating to reflect optional-append semantics | Risk: HIGH | Why: Union is the serialization contract for the MCP tool; adding a variant without proper discriminator wiring raises a Pydantic validation error at tool-call time\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::_sam_plan_create` (lines 271-296) - monolithic create path; must stay valid while new incremental path is added alongside it | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Current callers depend on all tasks being present in `tasks_yaml` at creation time; the new flow may change what fields are required\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::sam_plan` wrapper (~385-450) - must route the new `append` action to a new `_sam_plan_append_task` handler | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Routing logic is a match/dispatch on `PlanActionConfig` discriminator; missing branch silently falls through\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:9ab0ac27f806924be14903627a4a1644 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Understanding of `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` Protocol contract\\n- Understanding of `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` YAML I/O semantics (atomicity under concurrent readers)\\n- `tests_sam/` fixture style and test harness pattern\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Assessment**: NOT_APPLICABLE\\n\\n**Summary**: Net-new feature with no existing implementation to compare. Codebase shows no latent assumptions that would block the proposed incremental append API.\\n\\n**Why NOT_APPLICABLE**: This backlog item describes the creation of new API surface (`TaskBackend.append_task` method, `sam_plan(action='append_task')` routing, `AppendTaskConfig` discriminated union variant). The current implementation has none of these components, so there is no existing behavior to diverge from the design intent. The task is pure addition, not modification of an existing code path.\\n\\n**Latent assumptions verified** (no blockers found):\\n\\n- `CreatePlanConfig.tasks_yaml` accepts empty `{tasks: []}` today \u2014 no validation error will block the empty-plan-shell use case\\n- `_sam_plan_create` (lines 271-296) reads and validates `tasks_yaml` at runtime; monolithic path is isolated and regression-safe under the proposed design\\n- `TaskBackend` Protocol documentation (line 45-49) lists method groups but has no `append_task` stub yet; Protocol extension will not conflict with any existing method names\\n- `local_yaml` backend has `append_task_section` (line 497) as a precedent for task-level append semantics; pattern is established and reusable\\n- `github_task` backend maps tasks to sub-issues; appending post-creation is a novel GitHub API call pattern but no current code assumes tasks exist only at `create_plan` time\\n- Server routing in `sam_plan` wrapper dispatches via `PlanActionConfig` discriminator; adding new variant requires Pydantic union update but no implicit assumptions will break\\n\\n**No divergences detected \u2014 implementation can proceed as designed.**\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **make sam plans granular \u2014 incremental task append instead of monolithic create** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session on branch claude/add-sam-plan-plugin-uZTrQ (2026-04-12) \u2014 diagnosed streaming stall in another repo's Phase-4 planner\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-12)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a net-new feature item. No regression to reproduce.\\n\\nThe streaming-stall symptom that motivated this item can be observed by attempting to create a SAM plan with 16+ CLEAR+CoVe-compliant tasks in a single `sam_plan(action='create', tasks_yaml=...)` call:\\n\\n1. Open a session with the development-harness MCP server active.\\n2. Issue `sam_plan(action='create', ...)` with a `tasks_yaml` payload containing 16+ richly-specified tasks.\\n3. Observe: the tool_use block stalls mid-emission for ~90 seconds, then returns `API Error: Stream idle timeout - partial response received`.\\n4. Confirm: `sam_plan(action='list')` returns `count: 0` \u2014 no plan was persisted.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP0 \u2014 the streaming stall is a hard blocker for Phase-4 task decomposition on any plan with 16+ tasks. No workaround exists in the current API; agents cannot split the monolithic payload. This blocks all SAM-based planning at scale.\\n\\nEffort: L\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Unblocks SAM plans with 16+ tasks: the current monolithic `create` call fails silently for large plans; incremental append removes the payload-size ceiling entirely.\\n- Fixes the Phase-4 planner stall: agents that emit 16+ tasks in one `tasks_yaml` block will no longer experience the stream-idle timeout.\\n- Expands the applicable scope of `swarm-task-planner` and `task-decomposition` skill to arbitrarily large plans without workarounds.\\n- Three backends (`local_yaml`, `memory`, `github_task`) gain a new creation primitive that enables future tooling (partial-plan inspection, plan-building progress tracking) as a side effect.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Durability: the incremental path is inherently resilient to network interruption \u2014 each `append_task` call is a small, independently retriable unit.\\n- Future-proof API surface: once `TaskBackend.append_task` exists as a Protocol method, downstream tooling (progress bars, partial-plan reads, plan-building pipelines) can build on it without Protocol changes.\\n- Test confidence: smaller per-call surface area makes each `append_task` unit test simpler and more targeted than the current monolithic create test suite.\\n- Agent instruction clarity: agents no longer need to batch all tasks before any plan exists; they can write tasks as they are designed, reducing working-memory pressure during decomposition.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nOnce the feature ships, agents build a plan one task at a time using the following observable call sequence:\\n\\n1. `sam_plan(action='create', config={slug, goal, tasks_yaml='{tasks: []}'})` \u2014 creates an empty plan shell and returns the plan address (e.g. `P1`).\\n2. `sam_plan(action='append_task', plan='P1', task_yaml=<single-task YAML>)` \u2014 appends one task to the plan; called once per task; each call succeeds independently.\\n3. `sam_plan(action='read', plan='P1')` \u2014 round-trips to a plan structure identical to what a monolithic `create` with all tasks would have produced.\\n\\nThe existing monolithic `create` path (step 1 with all tasks in `tasks_yaml`) continues to work unchanged. Agents can choose either path; the resulting plan state is indistinguishable.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `sam_plan(action='create', tasks_yaml='{tasks: []}')` succeeds (returns plan address, no error) with an empty task list.\\n2. `sam_plan(action='append_task', plan=P, task_yaml=...)` appends a single task to plan P and returns a success acknowledgment.\\n3. After N sequential `append_task` calls, `sam_plan(action='read', plan=P)` returns a plan body structurally identical to what `create` with those same N tasks would have produced.\\n4. Existing monolithic `create` path is regression-safe: all existing `test_sam_create_*` tests continue to pass.\\n5. `TaskBackend.append_task` is implemented on all three backends: `local_yaml`, `memory`, `github_task`.\\n6. Each backend has unit test coverage for `append_task` including: happy path, plan-not-found error, and (where relevant) duplicate task ID handling.\\n7. `test_task_backend_conformance.py` includes `append_task` as a mandatory conformance case alongside `append_task_section`.\\n8. `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, `docs/backend-providers.md`, and `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` document the incremental append path.\\n9. `agents/swarm-task-planner.md` instructions are updated to describe the incremental append path as the preferred approach for plans with 16+ tasks.\\n\\n**Partial-plan semantics (resolved 2026-04-12, User decision):**\\n\\n10. Plans created via `sam_plan(action='create', tasks_yaml='{tasks: []}')` enter an explicit `drafting` state. Any plan currently being built via `append_task` remains in `drafting`.\\n11. `sam_plan(action='read', plan=P)` on a `drafting` plan returns the plan body including all tasks appended so far, and includes the `drafting` marker in the response.\\n12. `sam_plan(action='status', plan=P)` and `sam_plan(action='ready', plan=P)` on a `drafting` plan return a `drafting` marker instead of dispatchable task data. The plan is not yet available for execution.\\n13. A plan-review step clears the `drafting` marker: when review returns no-more-changes, the plan transitions to the executable state. While review requests changes, further `append_task` / `update` calls are permitted and the plan remains in `drafting`.\\n14. A new `sam_plan(action='finalize', plan=P)` routing OR an equivalent field-level transition clears the `drafting` marker. Implementer chooses the exact mechanism during planning; both options fit the existing Plan Pydantic model pattern.\\n15. `agents/plan-validator.md` is updated to treat `drafting` plans as valid intermediate states and defer full-plan checks (required-field coverage, DAG validity across all tasks) until `drafting` is cleared.\\n\\n**Concurrency contract (resolved 2026-04-12, User decision):**\\n\\n16. `TaskBackend.append_task` assumes a single writer per plan. Implementations are not required to be atomic under concurrent writers. The single-writer assumption is documented explicitly in the `TaskBackend.append_task` Protocol docstring.\\n17. `local_yaml` backend MAY use the same read-modify-rewrite pattern as existing methods (no file locking required). `github_task` MAY rely on GitHub's per-issue sequential semantics. `memory` backend needs no synchronization.\\n\\n**Regression test coverage:**\\n\\n18. New regression test `tests_sam/test_large_document_write.py` (or equivalent under existing test layout):\\n    - Test A: monolithic create with ~50 tasks (~40-80 KB `tasks_yaml`) completes and round-trips byte-for-byte\\n    - Test B: incremental create + 50 sequential `append_task` calls produces a plan with identical field content to Test A\\n    - Test C: mixed \u2014 create with 5 tasks, append 45 more, verify order and field preservation\\n19. New test coverage for `drafting` state transitions:\\n    - Test D: `status` and `ready` return `drafting` marker for a plan mid-append\\n    - Test E: `read` on a `drafting` plan returns task list plus `drafting` marker\\n    - Test F: after `finalize` (or equivalent clear), `status` and `ready` return normal dispatchable data\\n    - Test G: `plan-validator` accepts a `drafting` plan without raising false-negative errors\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 TaskBackend Protocol (method signatures, atomicity semantics) |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` lines 239-242 \u2014 PlanActionConfig discriminated union pattern |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` line 497 \u2014 `append_task_section` as existing append precedent |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py` lines 515-809+ \u2014 `test_sam_create_*` conformance suite as test template |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` line 283 \u2014 `append_task_section` conformance case as model for new `append_task` case |\\n| Agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 primary plan-creation agent; read to understand current instruction contract |\\n| Agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 reads plan structure; must be checked for partial-plan compatibility |\\n| Skill | `/dh:task-decomposition` \u2014 S4 skill that drives `sam_plan create`; must be updated |\\n| Doc | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` lines 99-101 \u2014 `plan_dir` gotcha section |\\n| Doc | `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 publisher-consumer map for SAM actions |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Producers (interface owners)**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 Protocol must gain `append_task` method\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 `PlanActionConfig` discriminated union must include new `AppendTaskConfig` variant\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 MCP routing must dispatch new `append_task` action\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Consumers (Protocol implementers)**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 must implement `append_task`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` \u2014 must implement `append_task`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` \u2014 must implement `append_task` via new sub-issue creation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/__init__.py` \u2014 verify re-exports\\n\\n**Tests**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_consolidated_tools.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py`\\n\\n**Documentation**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`\\n\\n**Agent Instructions**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md`\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Architectural decisions (resolved 2026-04-12 by User)**:\\n\\n1. **Concurrency**: `TaskBackend.append_task` assumes single-writer semantics. No locking required.\\n2. **Partial-plan state**: Plans enter a `drafting` state during append sequences; cleared by plan-review completion (no-more-changes) via a finalize mechanism.\\n\\n**Technical dependencies (all DERIVABLE, non-blocking)**:\\n- `ruamel.yaml` atomic write semantics in the `local_yaml` backend (existing usage in `local_yaml.py` is the reference)\\n- `tests_sam/` fixture style and test harness pattern (derivable from existing `test_sam_create_*` suite)\\n- `TaskBackend` Protocol contract (derivable by reading `task_backend.py` lines 38-278)\\n- `AppendTaskConfig` discriminated union wiring (derivable from existing Pydantic `Field(discriminator=)` pattern in `action_models.py`)\\n- `drafting` state representation \u2014 design choice between (a) adding a `drafting: bool` or `state: Literal[\\\"drafting\\\",\\\"ready\\\"]` field to the Plan Pydantic model, or (b) introducing a new `sam_plan(action='finalize')` routing. Both fit the existing pattern.\\n- `agents/plan-validator.md` update \u2014 must treat `drafting` as a valid intermediate state that defers full-plan validation until cleared.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nL (Large) \u2014 3-backend Protocol extension (including the novel GitHub sub-issue creation pattern), MCP server routing change, Pydantic discriminated union update, conformance test suite extension across 4 test files, documentation updates across 3 docs, and agent instruction updates across 3 agent/skill files. The `github_task` backend alone requires a new GitHub API call pattern with no existing test template.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` - explicitly documents `sam_plan(action='create')` as the required plan creation call (lines 259, 267, 270, 572); instructs agents to generate all tasks as a single YAML batch before calling create; the incremental flow requires updated instructions for when and how to use `append` | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the primary agent that creates SAM plans; if instructions still describe only monolithic create, the agent will never use the incremental path even after it ships\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` - documents `sam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"create\\\", ...})` as the plan creation call (line 125); must be updated if the incremental append changes when or how `create` is called | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Skill drives S4 task decomposition; stale instructions cause downstream agents to bypass the incremental path\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/sam-definition.md` - line 71 documents `sam_plan(action='create', slug, goal, tasks_yaml, issue)` as the registration call for task plans; needs updated to note the incremental alternative | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Referenced by work-backlog-item workflow; agents following this will always use the monolithic path\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/scope.md` - references `sam_plan create` indirectly | Risk: LOW | Why: Scope file is context-setting, not an operational call sequence; lower blast radius than the definition file\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` - validates SAM plans; if plan structure changes (tasks added incrementally), the validator must understand partial-plan state | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: A plan created with `create` + `append` may have a different task ordering or ID sequence; validator assertions could fail on valid incremental plans\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` - must implement `TaskBackend.append_task`; already has `append_task_section` (line 497) as a precedent pattern | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Method exists for section-level append but not task-level; the new method must reuse or extend that path without regressing existing `create_plan` semantics\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` - must implement `TaskBackend.append_task`; currently has `create_plan` (line 196) and `append_task_section` (line 456) | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: In-memory backend is used by all conformance tests; missing implementation causes Protocol conformance failure and breaks the test suite\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` - must implement `TaskBackend.append_task`; currently has `create_plan` (line 273) and `append_task_section` (line 439) | Risk: HIGH | Why: GitHub backend maps tasks to sub-issues; appending a task post-creation requires creating a new sub-issue atomically \u2014 this is a distinct GitHub API call pattern not currently exercised by any test in `tests_sam/`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/__init__.py` - may need to re-export new symbols if `AppendTaskConfig` or helper types are added to `action_models.py` | Risk: LOW | Why: Simple re-export; failure is an ImportError caught immediately at module load\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend_types.py` - type aliases and supporting types for `TaskBackend`; may need new input/output type for `append_task` return value | Risk: LOW | Why: Additive