nce remains valid but the SAM server section should mention `append` as a supported action | Risk: LOW | Why: The CLAUDE.md is a navigation aid, not an operational reference; low blast radius but could mislead orientation\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (partial-plan semantics defined for read/status/ready operations)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (plan-validator behavior on incremental plans)\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` - requires a novel GitHub API call pattern (create sub-issue on append post-plan-creation) with zero existing test coverage\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` - the primary plan-creation agent; if instructions are not updated, the incremental path will never be exercised even after it ships\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_consolidated_tools.py` + `tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` - no coverage for `append_task` on any backend; a silent no-op implementation would pass CI\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - verification: zero test coverage for the new `append` action path across all three backends and the MCP routing layer\\n  - compatibility: `PlanActionConfig` union extension requires Pydantic discriminator wiring; incorrect union definition raises at tool-call time\\n  - agent-instruction: three agent/skill files instruct monolithic YAML batch creation; stale instructions mean the feature is technically shipped but behaviorally unused\\n  - migration: no partial-plan state exists today; introducing it requires clear semantics for what \\\"a plan with appended tasks\\\" looks like at read/status/ready time\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `agents/plan-validator.md` was not in the original description but is in scope because it validates plan structure and may reject incrementally-built plans as malformed\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` | Role: producer | Connection: Protocol definition \u2014 must gain `append_task` method | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` | Role: producer | Connection: `PlanActionConfig` discriminated union \u2014 must include new `AppendTaskConfig` variant | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` | Role: producer | Connection: MCP server routing for `sam_plan` \u2014 must dispatch new `append` action | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Protocol implementer \u2014 must add `append_task` | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Protocol implementer (test double) \u2014 must add `append_task` | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Protocol implementer \u2014 GitHub sub-issue creation on append; novel API pattern | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/__init__.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: re-export module | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend_types.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: supporting types for Protocol | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/excep